cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite the interactor-gyre tree it is vendored from and the sinew-mocap/solve specification it ports.
title: sinew_align, the C port of sinew-mocap/solve's Align.lean rotation fitter (vendored)
abstract: >-
  V-Sekai-fire/interactor-gyre at 6e047600849cb4c78e28b9779cc30d386cabeb97
  (src/gen/sinew_align.c, sinew_align.h, test/unit/test_sinew_align.c),
  copied file for file: the direct C transcription, function for function,
  of sinew-mocap/solve's core/spec/Sinew/Align.lean (lean/Sinew here):
  det9 / mul9 / transpose9 on row-major 3x3 arrays, rodrigues (one pair),
  ns30 (a 30-iteration Newton-Schulz orthonormalisation of the covariance,
  two or more pairs), regularize, valid9, jacobi9 and the Jacobi-SVD kabsch
  fallback, finishAlign and align (targets[i] ~= R sources[i]). The unit
  test is AlignTest.lean's oracle: a 120-degree rotation (the unit
  quaternion (0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5) as a matrix) recovered at N=5, N=2 and
  N=1 to 1e-4. Local adaptations: none to the three files; sinew_align_cli.c
  (this tree) wraps sinew_align as a host command for the gates' analysis
  scripts (centres each point set on its own centroid, optionally a fit
  about y); guest/drape/similarity.h feeds it the centred cross-covariance
  through sinew_finish_align for the drape's fit phase, and drape.elf's
  drape_sinew_align_test runs the oracle in the guest. Rotations stay 3x3
  matrices throughout (AGENTS.md rule 11).
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: K. S. Ernest (iFire)
